ogmersfield Park, Hampshire, was an English landowner and British Army officer. St John-Mildmay was born in 1810, the son of Sir Henry St John-Mildmay, 4th Baronet and Charlotte Bouverie. He succeeded his father as baronet in 1848. He was commissioned an officer in the 2nd Dragoon Guards, where he advanced to major before he resigned. He was later Commanding Officer and later Honorary Colonel of the North Hampshire Yeomanry. Serving as High Sheriff of Hampshire in 1862, he was also\n\nAdditional extracted evidence from the SAME documents (not independent sources and not guaranteed true). Use alongside the original documents above.\n[{\"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0403-c03155277f52:d00\", \"card_id\": \"ramdocs-0403-c03155277f52:d00:c0\", \"entity\": \"Henry St John-Mildmay\", \"scope\": \"Baronetcy\", \"claim\": \"Henry St John-Mildmay became the Baronet in 1784.\", \"answer\": \"1784\", \"quote\": \"He succeeded to the baronetcy and Dogmersfield Park in 1784.\", \"original_document_number\": 1}, {\"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0403-c03155277f52:d01\", \"card_id\": \"ramdocs-0403-c03155277f52:d01:c0\", \"entity\": \"Henry St John-Mildmay\", \"scope\": \"Baronet\", \"claim\": \"Henry St John-Mildmay became the Baronet on 11 Nov. 1808.\", \"answer\": \"11 Nov. 1808\", \"quote\": \"He succeeded his father in the baronetcy on 11 Nov. 1808.\", \"original_document_number\": 2}, {\"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0403-c03155277f52:d02\", \"card_id\": \"ramdocs-0403-c03155277f52:d02:c0\", \"entity\": \"Henry St John-Mildmay\", \"scope\": \"became the Baronet\", \"claim\": \"Henry St John-Mildmay became the Baronet in 1848.\", \"answer\": \"1848\", \"quote\": \"He succeeded his father as baronet in 1848.\", \"original_document_number\": 3}]\nRAMDocs final output contract (overrides example output formats): Return JSON with accepted_answers (all correct SHORT answer strings, including multiple valid answers; empty list if unsupported) and explanation (reasoning). Do not put confidence, sources or explana